appendix."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"3.1.2 Synthetic measurements","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":462.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":71.0,"r":257.6666666666667,"t":479.0},"charspan":[0,28],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"3.1.2 Synthetic measurements"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The forward solution is generated with a time step of dt undersampled in time to 15ms, leading to a total of 56 measurements. From the solution of the forward problem; we simulate a PC-MRI acquisition by subsampling into a rectangular measurement resolution of [2mm, 2mm, 2mm] and then applying the process described in Section 2.1 with a venc of double the maximal velocity. The magnitude is modelled as dtmeas","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":381.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":69.66666666666667,"r":542.0,"t":456.3333333333333},"charspan":[0,411],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"The forward solution is generated with a time step of dt undersampled in time to 15ms, leading to a total of 56 measurements. From the solution of the forward problem; we simulate a PC-MRI acquisition by subsampling into a rectangular measurement resolution of [2mm, 2mm, 2mm] and then applying the process described in Section 2.1 with a venc of double the maximal velocity. The magnitude is modelled as dtmeas"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"1.0 if z is in the lumen of the vessel (16) 0.5 otherwise.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":341.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":233.66666666666666,"r":541.0,"t":371.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,58],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Finally a Gaussian noise € € CN is added with a signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) of 15. Fifty independent realizations of the noise were generated. complex","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":299.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.0,"r":540.0,"t":330.0},"charspan":[0,150],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"Finally a Gaussian noise € € CN is added with a signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) of 15. Fifty independent realizations of the noise were generated. complex"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Next, the sampling mask is applied to these simulated   frequency space measurements. We take a 2D subsampled mask in the 2 y-plane and sample fully in the z-direction as in [4]. We consider different subsampling rates R Nsampled 8,16,32, with two different Ntotal masks: the pseudo-spiral mask and the pseudo-random Gaussian mask, which is according to a Gaussian probability distribution; as shown in Figure 2 For the pseudo-spiral mask, the points are placed evenly on a cartesian along a spiral with six turns and final radius reaching the of the mask. sampled grid edge","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":96.04331995493465,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.33333333333333,"r":542.0230049071687,"t":199.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,574],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"Next, the sampling mask is applied to these simulated   frequency space measurements. We take a 2D subsampled mask in the 2 y-plane and sample fully in the z-direction as in [4]. We consider different subsampling rates R Nsampled 8,16,32, with two different Ntotal masks: the pseudo-spiral mask and the pseudo-random Gaussian mask, which is according to a Gaussian probability distribution; as shown in Figure 2 For the pseudo-spiral mask, the points are placed evenly on a cartesian along a spiral with six turns and final radius reaching the of the mask. sampled grid edge"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"For   comparison; we reconstructed velocity measurements   from these   synthetic measurements the Berkeley Advanced Reconstruction Toolbox  (BART) [11]. BART is command-line-based   software that provides à methods; as well as tools for simulation; pre-processing; and image reconstruction; providing a multitude of different regularization options. compressed sensing reconstructions of the velocities; using total variation in time as for the regularization. using","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":197.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":69.66666666666667,"r":542.0,"t":300.0},"charspan":[0,467],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":"For   comparison; we reconstructed velocity measurements   from these   synthetic measurements the Berkeley Advanced Reconstruction Toolbox  (BART) [11]. BART is command-line-based   software that provides à methods; as well as tools for simulation; pre-processing; and image reconstruction; providing a multitude of different regularization options. compressed sensing reconstructions of the velocities; using total variation in time as for the regularization. using"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"10","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":69.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":299.6666666666667,"r":313.6666666666667,"t":81.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,2],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/10","text":"10"}],"version":"1.10.0"}